      Last updated: September 2026 | 14 min read
    </p>

    <!-- Answer First -->
    <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> Anping County, in Hebei Province, is the world's largest wire mesh manufacturing cluster — an estimated 60% of China's wire mesh output and a dominant share of global supply comes from this single county of 500+ factories. The cluster exists because of 500 years of weaving heritage, a complete local supply chain (wire drawing, weaving, galvanizing, all within one industrial zone), and massive price advantages from fierce internal competition. If you buy wire mesh from China, you are almost certainly buying from Anping — whether you know it or not.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- TOC -->
