    <!-- Section 4: Quality Tiers -->
    <section id="tiers" class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">4. Quality Tiers: Not All Anping Factories Are Equal</h2>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        The most common mistake buyers make is treating "Anping wire mesh factory" as a single quality category. In reality, the cluster spans three distinct tiers with very different capabilities, certifications, and price points:
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-6">
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Tier 3: Volume Commodity</h3>
          <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>• Small workshops, 5–30 looms</li>
            <li> • Standard mesh counts only</li>
            <li> • GB/T standards, minimal testing</li>
            <li> • No export documentation support</li>
            <li> • <strong>Best for:</strong> Domestic trade, low-spec construction mesh</li>
            <li> • <strong>Price:</strong> Lowest (often 30–40% below export tier)</li>
            <li> • <strong>Risk:</strong> Inconsistent wire diameter, material substitution</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Tier 2: Export Standard</h3>
          <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>• Mid-size factories, 50–200 looms</li>
            <li> • ISO 9001 certified</li>
            <li> • ASTM E11 / ISO 9044 compliance</li>
            <li> • Mill certificates available</li>
            <li> • <strong>Best for:</strong> Standard B2B orders, distributors, contractors</li>
            <li> • <strong>Price:</strong> 10–20% below Western equivalents</li>
            <li> • <strong>Risk:</strong> Limited custom capability at extreme specs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Tier 1: Precision / Engineering</h3>
          <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>• Large manufacturers with R&D labs</li>
            <li> • ISO 9001 + 14001, some with ASME/CE</li>
            <li> • ±0.003mm wire tolerance capability</li>
            <li> • In-house PMI testing, filtration efficiency reports</li>
            <li> • <strong>Best for:</strong> Pharma, aerospace, oil & gas, food contact</li>
            <li> • <strong>Price:</strong> Comparable to Western suppliers, higher MOQs</li>
            <li> • <strong>Risk:</strong> Low — these factories supply OEM filter brands</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-2">The Key Insight</h3>
        <p class="text-theme-secondary">
          Roughly 70% of Anping factories are Tier 3, 25% are Tier 2, and only about 5% are Tier 1. Yet Tier 1 factories produce a disproportionate share of export value because they serve OEM and specification-driven markets. <strong>Your job as a buyer is to match your application's criticality to the right tier — and pay for only the tier you need.</strong> A chicken-fence supplier doesn't need a PMI lab; a pharmaceutical filter supplier can't operate without one.
        </p>
      </div>
